# Shell scripts must keep LF endings whatever a contributor's core.autocrlf is
# set to. A CRLF shebang makes the kernel look for an interpreter named "bash\r",
# which fails as "bad interpreter: No such file or directory" — an error that
# names neither the file nor the real cause. docker/Dockerfile.psn and
# Dockerfile.psn-spike already run dos2unix to work around exactly this.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning: these are read by tools that will not tolerate CRLF.
Dockerfile* text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts keep CRLF.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Never touch binary or signed material.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.p12 binary
*.cer binary
